 against the counts on record\n2302:## 5. `β⁺` by simulation: the width of explicit constructions at large `n` (item 05, 2026-11-01)\n2382:### 5.1 Findings\n2504:### 5.2 Kill verdict\n2521:### 5.3 What this does not claim\n2544:### 5.4 Figure\n2554:### 5.5 Tables, in full\n2562:#### beta+ per construction and cell, with beta* and b\n2603:#### The fits in full\n2644:#### Per cell and n: width / n of every construction\n2852:#### Fitted cells not accepted within the draw cap\n5000 |  0.5 |   2 |      20 |          3.28  |\n| fitted      | 5000 |  0.5 |   3 |      20 |          2.71  |\n| fitted      | 5000 |  0.5 |   4 |      20 |          2.12  |\n| fitted      | 5000 |  1   |   2 |      20 |          4.9   |\n| fitted      | 5000 |  1   |   3 |      20 |          4.01  |\n\n M Ralph_Loops/loop0010/iterations.md\n M Ralph_Loops/loop0010/loop.log\n M Ralph_Loops/loop0010/nohup.out\n M Ralph_Loops/loop0010/status.json\n M learning/excess.py\n M reports/excess_phase_diagram.md\n?? Ralph_Loops/loop0010/gate_it05.log\n?? Ralph_Loops/loop0010/session_it05.jsonl\n?? Ralph_Loops/loop0010/session_it05.log\n?? learning/excess_constructions.py\n?? reports/figures/excess_beta_plus.png\n?? reports/scratch/excess_constructions/\n?? tests/test_excess_constructions.py","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/excess_constructions/section_body.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":171,"newStart":1,"newLines":0,"lines":["-","-### 5.1 Findings","-","-1. **The run.** 2,043 rows, 2,024 accepted instances (1,080 fixed, 944","-   fitted), `n = 100–5000`, 36 cells; 1.61 core-hours of instance time, 751 s","-   wall on 8 workers at `nice -n 19` (load 1–9), under the item's 8. The rule","-   is 98% of the time (`O(n²)` in Python with popcounts: 0.2 s at `n = 1000`,","-   1.3 s at 2000, 11–22 s at 5000, by `m`); the BFS layout, the greedy","-   independent set and the edge count together are 0.003 core-hours. Every","-   instance is fresh; nothing was solved, `solutions/` and the ledger are","-   untouched. Within a cell the rule's `width / n` has standard deviation","-   0.016–0.022 at `n = 100` and 0.002–0.003 at 5000.","-","-2. **The rule's `width / n` falls with `n` in every cell, and the `1 / n`","-   form fits it.** Against item 02's expectation (that the rule's excess per","-   customer, which grows with `n` relative to the optimum at `n ≤ 100`, would","-   drift `rule / n` *upward*), `rule / n` decreases monotonically from","-   `n = 100` to 5000 in all 36 cells — e.g. `(4, 1)`: 0.419, 0.406, 0.404,","-   0.400, 0.395, 0.393; `(3, 1)`: 0.276 → 0.237; `(2, 2)`: 0.223 → 0.191 —","-   and the residuals of `width / n = β⁺ + a / n` per size are within","-   ±0.009 with no sign pattern. Fitting `1 / √n` or `log n / n` instead","-   moves `β⁺` by at most 0.010 (0.006–0.010 lower for `1 / √n`, 0.001–0.002","-   for `log n / n`) with residual sums of squares within 10% of each other,","-   so the extrapolated constant is insensitive to the form at the 0.01","-   level. The intercept `a` is 1–8 stacks (largest on the ridge, `(3, 1)`,","-   `(4, 1)`, `(6, ½)`), the same order as item 02's certified intercepts","-   (3–9), which is why `rule / n` at `n ≤ 100` overstates the slope by","-   0.03–0.08 and `rule / n` at 5000 by 0.01–0.06. Both statements are about","-   the rule's own width, which is a layout of each instance: how far it is","-   from the optimum at `n = 5000` is not known, since nothing there is","-   certified.","-","-3. **The rule's `β⁺` sits 0.01–0.06 above the certified slope `b`, and the","-   gap is smallest at the two ends of the excess.** Fixed generator,","-   `rule β⁺ − b` (standard errors of `β⁺` 0.001–0.010, of `b` 0.002–0.011):","-","-   | `μ` \\ `d` | 2 | 3 | 4 | 6 | 8 | 10 |","-   |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","-   | ½ | 0.039 | 0.055 | 0.040 | 0.054 | 0.060 | 0.051 |","-   | 1 | 0.017 | 0.037 | 0.047 | 0.031 | 0.027 | 0.014 |","-   | 2 | 0.024 | 0.037 | 0.037 | 0.020 | 0.010 | 0.007 |","-","-   and for the fitted generator at `μ = 1` against the Chu & Stuckey classes","-   it was fitted to: `d = 2` 0.040, 4 0.035, 6 0.024, 8 0.020, 10 0.013. At","-   `μ = 1` and `2` the gap peaks at `d = 3–4` (`e = 2–3`, the ridge and its","-   dense shoulder) and falls to 0.007–0.017 at the ends; at `μ = ½` it is","-   0.04–0.06 everywhere, as item 02 found the rule worst at small `μ`. The","-   order `b < rule β⁺` holds in every cell and `rule β⁺` sits *below* the","-   certified `opt / n` at the largest small `n` (75–125) in every cell: the","-   rule at `n = 5000` is per customer better than the exact optimum at","-   `n ≤ 125`, consistent with `opt / n` still falling there (item 02 §2.3).","-","-4. **The two proved constructions are far from `β*`, and which one is better","-   switches at `e ≈ 2–2.5`.** `n − α_greedy` is flat in `n` to ±0.005 in","-   every cell (a law of large numbers; item 07's differential-equation limit","-   is what it converges to) and runs from 0.48 (`(2, 1)`) to 0.96","-   (`(10, 2)`); the edge-count bound `|E| / 5.769 ≈ μ C(d, 2) / 5.769` per","-   customer is below `n − α` only on the sparse side — 0.22 against 0.48 at","-   `(2, 1)`, 0.24 against 0.58 at `(2, ½)`, 0.35 against 0.54 at `(2, 2)`,","-   0.55 against 0.61 at `(3, 1)`, 0.62 against 0.66 at `(4, ½)` — and above","-   1 from `(4, 1)`, `(3, 2)`, `(6, ½)` on. The best proved `β⁺` minus `β*`","-   is 0.075 at `(10, 2)`, 0.11–0.23 at `d ≥ 8`, 0.16–0.42 at `d = 4–6`, and","-   0.22–0.62 at `d ≤ 3` (where `β* = 0`, the bound is the whole number);","-   item 07's kill (`β⁺ − β* > 0.5` everywhere) is therefore **not** met —","-   the gap is below 0.5 on 29 of 36 cells and below 0.2 on 11 — but on no","-   cell is a proved construction within 0.07 of the first moment.","-","-5. **The BFS layout is between the rule and `n − α` everywhere but in the","-   sparse regime, where it is the only construction whose width is","-   sublinear.** Its exact vertex separation per customer is flat in `n`","-   (±0.03, noisier than the others since one random root decides it) at","-   0.13–0.96, 1.1–2.5× the rule's; the layer bound `max (|L_i| + |L_{i+1}|) − 1`","-   is 0.35–1.0 per customer and never the binding quantity (two consecutive","-   layers of a BFS tree on a graph of mean degree `μ d (d − 1) ≥ 4` hold most","-   of the vertices). The exception is the fixed `(2, ½)` cell, `e = 0.87`","-   (between `e_g(½) = 0.5` and 1, 652 components of mean size 7.7 at","-   `n = 5000`): the BFS separation per customer falls 0.073, 0.044, 0.022,","-   0.013, 0.010, 0.005 from `n = 100` to 5000 (about `n^{−0.7}`; 25 stacks","-   at `n = 5000`), while **the rule stays at 0.043–0.066** (215 stacks at","-   `n = 5000`, `β⁺ = 0.044 ± 0.004` against a certified `b = 0.005 ± 0.006`","-   at `n = 50–75`). On many-component sparse instances the two-key rule's","-   width is linear in `n` where a trivial layout's is not; the mechanism","-   is not analysed here (the rule's first key counts newly opened","-   neighbours and nothing in it closes a component before starting the","-   next). At `(2, 1)` (`e = 1.14`, 128 components) the BFS is 0.13 against","-   the rule's 0.054, so the crossover is below `e ≈ 1.1`.","-","-6. **The fitted generator does not exist at large `n` and small `d`.** Its","-   rejection step discards disconnected instances, and the expected number","-   of isolated pattern pairs is linear in `n` at fixed density, so the","-   acceptance probability falls like `exp(−c n)`: no draw of `(2, ½)` was","-   accepted from `n = 200` (1,000 tries), of `(3, ½)` from 1,000 (5 of 10 at","-   500), of `(4, ½)` and `(2, 1)` from 2,000, of `(3, 1)` at 5,000 (20","-   tries, 4 s each); 19 of 2,043 rows, 15 `(n, μ, d)` cells. Where it is","-   accepted its realised excess is above the nominal `μ (d − 1)` by the","-   padding — `(2, 1)` 1.64 against 1.0, `(4, 1)` 3.14 against 3.0, `(2, 2)`","-   3.10 against 2.0 — and its constructions sit 0.00–0.05 above the fixed","-   generator's at equal `(d, μ)` (rule `β⁺` fitted − fixed: `(4, 1)` 0.035,","-   `(6, 1)` 0.015, `(10, 1)` 0.008, `(10, 2)` 0.005), the difference","-   shrinking with `d` as the realised sizes concentrate. The Chu & Stuckey","-   `d = 2` classes — the sparse flank, where SCOOP lives — are a finite-size","-   object under their own generator: at 125 customers the acceptance is","-   still a few percent (§4 of `REPORT_generator.md`), at 2,000 it is zero","-   in 100 tries.","-","-7. **What the table says about the constant.** On the 11 trusted cells","-   (finding 8) the three numbers are ordered `β* < b < rule β⁺` with","-   `rule β⁺ − β*` 0.02–0.10 and `b − β*` 0.01–0.06; the rule's extrapolated","-   per-customer width is the best *measured* upper envelope on record for","-   `lim opt / n` at `n → ∞`, and the first moment the only lower one. The","-   provable sandwich is `β* ≤ lim inf opt / n ≤ lim sup opt / n ≤ min(1 −","-   α_greedy / n, μ C(d, 2) / 5.769)` with the right side 0.08–0.6 above the","-   left; item 07's job is to prove the limits of `n − α_greedy` and of the","-   BFS layer fractions, and the table says in advance that neither will be","-   within 0.07 of `β*` anywhere.","-","-### 5.2 Kill verdict","-","-**Met on 12 of the 23 cells with a certified `b`; 11 trusted; 13 untested.**","-The rule's `width / n` at the largest `n` reached and item 02's slope `b` at","-`n ≤ 100` differ by more than 0.03 on all six `μ = ½` cells (0.038–0.062),","-on `(3, 1)` 0.037, `(4, 1)` 0.045, `(3, 2)` 0.035, `(4, 2)` 0.037, and on","-the fitted `(2, 1)` 0.040 and `(4, 1)` 0.037: **those twelve extrapolations","-are not trusted and later items may not quote them.** Trusted (difference","-≤ 0.03): fixed `(2, 1)` 0.016, `(6, 1)` 0.030, `(8, 1)` 0.027, `(10, 1)`","-0.014, `(2, 2)` 0.024, `(6, 2)` 0.020, `(8, 2)` 0.010, `(10, 2)` 0.007;","-fitted `(6, 1)` 0.024, `(8, 1)` 0.021, `(10, 1)` 0.012. The 13 cells with no","-certified series at `n ≤ 100` (the fitted generator at `μ = ½` and `2`, and","-`(3, 1)`) are untested and not to be quoted either. The pattern is the one","-item 04 predicted: the criterion fails on the sparse flank and the ridge,","-where the rule is worst, and at every `μ = ½` cell; it passes at `e ≥ 5` and","-at `(2, 1)`, `(2, 2)`.","-","-### 5.3 What this does not claim","-","-- **A limit.** `β⁺` is the intercept of a least-squares line in `1 / n`","-  through six sizes, the largest 5,000; the form was checked against two","-  alternatives (0.01 agreement), not derived. Nothing at `n > 125` is","-  certified, so whether `opt / n` approaches `b`, `rule β⁺` or something","-  else is open; the rule's number is the width of one layout per instance.","-- **A bound, except two.** Only `n − α_greedy` (`IndependenceBound.lean`,","-  `pathwidth_le_card_sub_indepNum`, with `α ≥ α_greedy`) and `|E| / 5.769`","-  (Kneis et al. 2009, abstract, `O(log n)` omitted) are proved upper bounds,","-  and only on the instances where they were computed; the rule and the BFS","-  layout are upper bounds on those instances too, as layouts, but their","-  per-customer values at other `n` are not.","-- **The rule's quality at large `n`.** Its `width / n` falls with `n`; the","-  optimum's may fall faster (it did at `n ≤ 100`), so no statement about the","-  rule's gap at `n = 5000` is made.","-- **Anything about `(d, μ)` off the grid, `n` off `[100, 5000]`, or the","-  fitted generator where it was not accepted.** The 13 untested fitted cells","-  and the 12 killed cells are tabulated for the record, not for quotation.","-- **The mechanism of finding 5.** That the rule's width is linear and the","-  BFS layout's sublinear on the `(2, ½)` cell is measured on 60 instances;","-  why is not analysed.","-","-### 5.4 Figure","-","-`reports/figures/excess_beta_plus.png`: one panel per `μ`, against `d`;","-filled markers the fixed generator's `β⁺` per construction (bars ± 2 se,","-smaller than the markers), hollow markers the fitted generator's, the grey","-line `β*(d, μ)` at the nominal `d`, black ticks item 02's certified `b`.","-The edge-count bound leaves the frame at `d ≥ 4` (it is above 1 there).","-Palette: the dataviz reference order (blue, orange, aqua, yellow),","-validated.","-","-### 5.5 Tables, in full","-","-`python -m learning.excess --stage constructions-tables`","-(`reports/scratch/excess_constructions/tables.md`).","-"]}],"deleted":true},{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/excess_constructions/section_header.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":79,"newStart":1,"newLines":0,"lines":["-## 5. `β⁺` by simulation: the width of explicit constructions at large `n` (item 05, 2026-11-01)","-","-**Question.** B(ii), first half, of the plan. For the random cover model at","-fixed `(d, μ)` — `m = μ n` patterns of about `d` customers each — what width","-per customer do *explicit* layouts reach as `n` grows past anything the exact","-solver certifies? Four constructions, two of them proved bounds: the two-key","-closing rule (the default upper-bound seed; a layout of the instance, measured","-and not analysed), the BFS-layer layout (a layout of the instance, with the","-deterministic layer bound `max_i (|L_i| + |L_{i+1}|) − 1` beside its exact","-vertex separation), `n − α_greedy` (`pathwidth_le_card_sub_indepNum` of","-`IndependenceBound.lean` with `α ≥ α_greedy`, so a proved upper bound on the","-pathwidth of that instance), and the edge-count bound `|E| / 5.769` of Kneis,","-Mölle, Richter & Rossmanith (2009), cited as the survey","-(`reports/random_graph_pathwidth_survey.md` §1.4) cites it — abstract only,","-`pw ≤ |E| / 5.769 + O(log n)`, the `O(log n)` term omitted as the survey's","-table omits it. Per construction and cell the fit `width / n = β⁺ + a / n`,","-beside item 02's certified slope `b` at `n ≤ 100` and the first-moment","-constant `β*(d, μ)`.","-","-**What was done.** `learning/excess_constructions.py` (stages","-`constructions`, `constructions-tables`, `figure-constructions` of","-`learning.excess`), `tests/test_excess_constructions.py` (10 tests: the","-open-stack sweep against `mosp.verify.max_open_stacks` and the vertex","-separation against brute force on 200 random instances each, the rule's value","-against `two_key_rule`, BFS layers as a partition with every edge within one","-layer, the greedy independent set independent and maximal, every proved","-construction above the certified optimum minus one on 20 solved instances,","-seeds, the fit on a synthetic law, the tables on a synthetic frame).","-","-- **Fresh instances, nothing solved.** Two generators at `d ∈ {2, 3, 4, 6, 8,","-  10}`, `μ ∈ {½, 1, 2}`, `n ∈ {100, 200, 500, 1000, 2000, 5000}`, 10 instances","-  per cell, seeds deterministic per `(generator, n, μ, d, index)`: the","-  fixed-size generator `benchmarks.generator.generate_structured_instance`","-  (exactly `d` customers per pattern, empty customers padded to one pattern —","-  the generator of the certified ensemble series item 02 fitted), and the","-  fitted Chu & Stuckey generator of","-  `reports/scratch/clique_cover_moment/gen_candidates.py`","-  (`bern_padC1_padP2_conn`: Bernoulli(`d / n`) entries, customers padded to","-  ≥ 1 pattern, patterns to ≥ 2 customers, disconnected instances discarded).","-  The fitted generator's rejection cannot be honoured at large `n` and small","-  `d`: the expected number of isolated pattern pairs grows linearly in `n` at","-  fixed density, so the acceptance probability falls like `exp(−c n)`. The","-  draw cap is 2,000 at `n = 100`, 1,000 at 200, 500 at 500, 200 at 1,000, 100","-  at 2,000 and 20 at 5,000; one probe draw per cell first, and a cell whose","-  probe is not accepted within the cap is recorded as not accepted and never","-  forced. No instance went through any solver; `solutions/` and the compute","-  ledger are untouched.","-- **Per instance**: `n`, `m`, `n_ones`, realised `e`, `|E|` and the component","-  count of the MOSP graph, the pattern-size histogram; the rule's stacks and","-  `rule = stacks − 1`; the BFS layout's exact vertex separation, the layer","-  bound and the number of layers (layers of the MOSP graph from a uniformly","-  random root, a new random root for every further component, listed layer by","-  layer); `α_greedy` (minimum remaining degree) and `n − α_greedy`;","-  `|E| / 5.769`; seconds for each. Width is in **pathwidth units** throughout","-  (`optimum = pathwidth + 1`, so per-customer values agree with `opt / n` to","-  `1 / n`; the fit absorbs the constant).","-- **Per cell and construction**: `β⁺` and its standard error from the least","-  squares fit of `width / n` on `1 / n` over every instance of the cell (so","-  the error carries the within-cell spread); `width / n` at the largest `n`","-  reached; `β*(d, μ)` at the nominal `d` and at the realised size histogram of","-  the largest `n`; item 02's `b` — the fixed generator's own series at","-  `n = 30–100` for the fixed cells, the Chu & Stuckey `m = n` classes at","-  `n = 30–125` for the fitted `μ = 1` cells (the generator was fitted to","-  them); and the kill flag.","-","-**Size range.** `n = 100–5000`, `m = n / 2` to `2 n`; `e` from 0.5 to 18.","-`b` is from `n = 30–100` (30–125 for the Chu & Stuckey classes).","-","-**Regenerate.**","-","-```","-python -m learning.excess --stage constructions          # the grid -> learning/data/excess_constructions.csv","-python -m learning.excess --stage constructions-tables   # the tables below","-python -m learning.excess --stage figure-constructions   # reports/figures/excess_beta_plus.png","-python -m learning.excess_constructions --n 1000 --reps 1 --d 10 --mu 2   # one cell, for timing","-python -m pytest tests/test_excess_constructions.py -q","-```","-","-Run log: `reports/scratch/excess_constructions/run.log`."]}],"deleted":true},{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/Ralph_Loops/loop0010/iterations.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":181,"oldLines":7