{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgbTgay11NK8P6JazRPzs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 05 is done; eight items remain unchecked, so no LOOP_COMPLETE line. Nothing is committed, nothing under `solutions/` was touched, and no stray files sit outside the item's paths.\n\n**What was done.** `learning/excess_constructions.py` runs fresh random covers at 36 `(d, μ)` cells and `n = 100–5000`, 10 per cell, from both generators, and scores four constructions per instance: the two-key rule, the BFS-layer layout's exact vertex separation with the layer bound, `n − α_greedy`, and the edge-count bound. It then fits `width / n = β⁺ + a / n` per cell beside `β*` and item 02's certified slope `b`. 2,024 accepted instances in 1.6 core-hours, no exact solve. Ten new tests pass, and the gate passed in one run.\n\n**Findings.**\n- The rule's `width / n` falls with `n` in every cell, against item 02's expectation of an upward drift. The `1 / n` form fits with residuals within 0.009, and the extrapolated constant moves by at most 0.01 under two alternative forms.\n- The rule's `β⁺` sits 0.007 to 0.060 above the certified slope. The gap is smallest at both ends of the excess and largest on the ridge and at every `μ = ½` cell.\n- The proved constructions are far from the first moment. `n − α_greedy` runs 0.48 to 0.96 per customer, the edge bound is only better below `e ≈ 2.5`, and no proved construction comes within 0.07 of `β*` on any cell.\n- On the sparse many-component cell `(2, ½)` the rule's width is linear in `n` while the BFS layout's is sublinear. At `n = 5000` that is 215 stacks against 25.\n- The fitted Chu & Stuckey generator cannot be realised at large `n` and small `d`, since its connectivity rejection accepts with probability falling like `exp(−c n)`.\n\n**Kill verdict: met on 12 of 23 cells.** Those extrapolations, and the 13 cells with no certified series, are not to be quoted by later items. Eleven cells are trusted, all at `e ≥ 5` or at `d = 2` with `μ ≥ 1`.\n\n**Next** is item 06, the forest regime on paper. The PROGRESS entry records what items 07 to 12 should take from this one."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":714,"cache_read_input_tokens":232897,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":714,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":787,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba2660ed-54b6-4b2f-a3ea-6cf6617bc43b","uuid":"41188d26-8d07-4b67-a9eb-56cca41c152e","timestamp":"2026-11-01T03:00:09.877Z","request_id":"req_011CgbTgabfjE86iyhiPwkrp"}
